WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.267
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.968
We used to talk when you used to
come on "Late Night,"

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:05.400
and you used to say like,

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.000
"Yeah, I'm going to be
going to space one day.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.601
I'm going to go to space."
And you're doing it now.

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:11.701
You did it.
-Yeah, it was --

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:13.467
Many years
I think we did interviews,

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.534
and I would go "next year,"
"next year," "next year."

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:17.567
But anyway, finally it happened.

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:20.300
-Here you are in space.
-Yeah, it was --

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:25.601
-You said you were gonna do it,
and then you did it.

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:27.801
-It was the most extraordinary
day of my life.

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:32.467
And it was a real
"pinch me" moment.

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:36.167
And it's just --
I hope all of you one day

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:39.901
have the chance to go to space,
and that's our challenge.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:42.067
-I mean, you think that --
You think that

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:44.000
there will come a day
where that...?

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.267
-Well, I think -- You know,

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:46.934
we're building
a number of spaceships,

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.868
another number of motherships.

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:52.734
And there are others
trying to do the same thing.

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:55.601
And I think in time
the price will come down

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:57.968
so that, you know,
hopefully more and more people

00:00:57.968 --> 00:01:00.567
will have a chance,
but it'll be --

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:02.734
it'll be a number of years

00:01:02.734 --> 00:01:04.334
before a lot of people
have a chance.

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:06.467
-What was your takeaway?
Were you scared at all?

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:10.367
-I wasn't scared for one second
of the whole day.

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:12.701
I just was so looking
forward to it.

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:16.067
And I had my kids
and grandkids there,

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:18.868
and it was just
a dream come true.

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:20.501
-The Virgin Group
does so many different things.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:22.868
You do -- You go to space,
you have hotels,

00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:24.868
you have cruise ships.

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:28.467
How do you decide what is the
thing you're gonna be into?

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:32.734
-Generally out of frustration
I mean, if I, I mean --

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:35.501
the way I started Virgin
Atlantic nearly 40 years ago

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:38.701
was I was trying to get
to the Virgin Islands.

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:41.334
I got bumped off a flight.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:44.300
I went to the back of
the airport and hired a plane.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.734
I went, got a blackboard,

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:48.100
I wrote as a joke,
"Virgin Airlines. One way.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.634
$39 to the British
Virgin Islands."

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:52.834
Went out to all the passengers
that got bumped.

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:55.834
And I filled up my first plane.
And...

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:59.334
-That's -- Easy as that.
Now you have your own airline.

00:01:59.334 --> 00:02:01.267
How many years ago was that?

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:04.133
-That was 39. 39 years ago.
-39 years ago. Yeah.

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:06.000
Still going strong.
-The next day, rang Boeing

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.501
and asked if they had
any secondhand 747s for sale.

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:13.200
-But this whole thing --
I've read your story,

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.567
and it's a fascinating story.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:17.167
But from what I remember,
I think this whole thing started

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:19.567
with a necklace
that your mother found?

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:22.267
-Yeah, I was trying
to start a magazine

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:24.167
to campaign against
the Vietnamese War,

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:27.634
which, like most wars,
I thought was a very unjust war.

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:29.667
And -- And --

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:31.801
[ Applause ]

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:32.968
Uh...

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:36.133
And I was 15 going on 16.

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:38.234
I was working from
the school phone box.

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:40.234
And my mom found a necklace.

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:42.968
Because we didn't have
much money.

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:45.767
She handed it in to the police.
Nobody claimed it.

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:50.501
And I was given by my mum
the $200 to use in the phone box

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:53.767
to try to get the advertising
to start the magazine.

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:55.801
And that was, you know --

00:02:55.801 --> 00:03:00.734
That was really our complete
funding to build the magazine,

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:03.100
then to start building
Virgin Records,

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.067
and one thing led on to another.

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:06.901
-Yeah. Wow.

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:09.367
-So, very grateful to my mum.
-Thank you, Mum. Yeah, exactly.

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:12.367
Yeah. Oh, that's wild.
-Yeah.

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:15.634
-Thank you to whoever was good
enough to leave their necklace.

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:17.334
-Yeah, exactly. Right.

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:20.167
And so now let's talk about
the hotel here in New York.

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:23.567
-Yeah, I mean, Virgin's
been flying to New York.

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:26.634
I mean, we have maybe 12 flights
a day to New York.

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:29.467
-It's most fun airline.
It's the best.

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:31.734
The colors are fun.
Everything's cool about it.

00:03:31.734 --> 00:03:32.968
You go, "Yeah."
I always loved it.

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:34.334
-Well, thank you.

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:36.534
And when people
get off the plane,

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:39.100
they have to go
to dark and dingy hotels,

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.367
which I'm afraid quite a lot
of hotels in New York are.

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:43.601
There are some good ones.

00:03:43.601 --> 00:03:46.434
And so we thought we'd open one

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:49.100
with massive windows
in every room,

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.467
beautiful views
of the Empire State Building

00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:53.701
and the rest of New York,
and did it

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:55.534
with a delightful man
called John Lam.

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:59.234
And we're very, very, very
happy the way it's turned out.

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:01.300
-Where'd you open it?

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:05.133
-It's on Broadway,
and it's just off Times Square,

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.501
where we've had
quite a lot of history with,

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:10.400
you know, Virgin Megastores
and other things.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:13.467
-I know you had the cast
of "New York, New York."

00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:16.567
-We had the cast
out on the street today.

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:18.467
We rang up the police
and said, "Look.

00:04:18.467 --> 00:04:20.334
Would you mind
closing the street

00:04:20.334 --> 00:04:22.100
while we've got the cast
from 'New York, New York'"?

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.400
-They're like, "We're a little
busy today closing the streets.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:29.400
Of all days? No! Tomorrow
we'll do it. Why today?"

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.767
-What they said was, "We've had
to close the rest of New York.

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:33.534
So what's one more street.?"

00:04:33.534 --> 00:04:36.334
-[ Laughs ]
That is so funny.

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:38.534
That's funny. That's great.
-They gave us permission.

00:04:38.534 --> 00:04:41.067
-That's great. Congratulations
on the new hotel.

00:04:41.067 --> 00:04:42.934
And we always love
having you here.

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:45.334
You're such a great spirit.
Good to see you, buddy.

00:04:45.334 --> 00:04:47.501
-Thank you.
-Sir Richard Branson.

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:50.701
Virgin Hotels New York City
is officially open now.

00:04:50.701 --> 00:04:54.467
For more information,
go to VirginHotels.com/nyc.

00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:57.300
More "Tonight Show" after the
break. Stick around, everybody.

